<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in May.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in May.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building approvals rose a seasonally-adjusted 2.2 percent in May to 12,327 from 12,062 in April, compared with 10,736 in May 1996, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The bureau said approvals for private sector houses rose 6.3 percent in May, due entirely to approval for the Olympic Games Village in Sydney, which comprises 1,021 new houses and 540 other residential units.</p>
<p>Economists on average had expected building approvals to rise 2.0 percent.  </p>
<p>Australian housing building approvals-</p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJUSTED		   May 97  April 97   May 96</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  8,781    8,257    6,890</p>
<p>    Total houses			     8,910    8,419    7,016</p>
<p>    Total private dwelling units	12,049   11,684   10,380</p>
<p>    Total dwelling units		  12,327   12,062   10,736</p>
<p>    Value residential building (A$ bln) 1.45     1.53     1.25</p>
<p>    Value total buildings (A$ bln)	2.35     2.27     2.26</p>
<p>TREND ESTIMATES</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  8,257     8,135    7,086</p>
<p>    Total Dwelling Units		  12,147    12,132   10,485</p>
